WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.622
There is no universal industry definition of a small, medium, or large language model.

00:00:06.622 --> 00:00:09.947
The ranges here are teaching shorthand.

00:00:09.947 --> 00:00:15.512
Below roughly four billion parameters is a useful small-model category.

00:00:15.512 --> 00:00:20.102
Around four to fourteen billion is a practical medium range.

00:00:20.102 --> 00:00:24.802
Roughly fifteen to forty billion represents heavier local models,

00:00:24.802 --> 00:00:32.912
and still larger models or mixture-of-experts systems often require distributed or managed infrastructure.

00:00:32.912 --> 00:00:41.157
The exact deployment fit depends on architecture, active parameters, quantization, context length, and hardware.

00:00:41.157 --> 00:00:45.440
Parameter count is only the first estimate.
